2. THE APPLICABLE OPERATING STATE OF A SUPERVISOR (U41, U51, U61, STM32H743VIT6), AS THE TREE DEFINES IT
   v2/docs/HW-FW-CONTRACT.md: 11 rows name the supervisors (their I2C target addresses, CAN FD at 1 Mbps or less, the quorum, the vote rate);
     rows that bound a run mode, a clock or a voltage scale: NONE
   v2/docs/PANEL.md: rows that bound them: NONE
   v2/docs/ARCH-PCB-B-IOHA.md (Power): 'roughly 60 mA each at 3.3 V with the core clocked to what CAN-FD timing needs, not to 480 MHz': an INTENT, with no clock,
     no voltage scale, no acceptance and no measured or printed current (DECLARED, architecture text)
   v2/ecad/tools/gen_sch_b.py: a 25 MHz crystal a controller (HSE); each +3V3_IOCx DECLARED 0.12 A typical, 0.25 A peak, its loads 0.060 A for
     the controller and 0.020 A for each of its three other parts
   firmware in the tree: v2/firmware holds panel only: NO supervisor firmware
   rv-pwr's budget (the case's loads): 33 / 71 / 400 mA a controller (LOW, PLAN, HIGH) plus 60 mA of its other parts (DECLARED)
   FINDING: THE STATE IS UNBOUNDED. Nothing in the tree defines, limits or tests a supervisor's run mode, clock or voltage scale; the
     architecture's 60 mA is an intent, and the part runs whatever its firmware sets, up to the worst state its sheet prints

